A||N||8||superXmotorsports||trouble shifting 5 spd when warm...||||5||
Z||000000||superXmotorsports||07-22-2000||05:49 PM||||Hi eveyone.  I picked up another GT w/ 5spd and a newer clutch.  The cars shifts great when its cold but after a few minutes of driving it won't go into gear.  If you turn the car off it will immediately go into gear.  Any thoughts?  Thanks!  SXM.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula||07-22-2000||05:57 PM||||I was going to say clutch but you said its new.......hmmmmmmm..... sorry, I cant help on this one||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||07-22-2000||07:08 PM||||It's the oil.  Make sure that you have 5W30 engine oil in there and not gear oil.  When my tranny was rebuilt the shop put gear oil into it and when it got hot I could not shift either.  Than after changing to proper oil it worked.  <BR>If it stinks it's gear oil so try that.<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||07-23-2000||02:52 AM||||I filled mine up with 85w-140 gear oil. Switching to 5-30 will actually make a noticeable difference when shifting?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sillhouette.com||07-23-2000||10:03 AM||||YES make sure that your tranny is running with 5W30 engine oil.  It was not build to take the thick stuff.  Anytime you have problem shifting or you're grinding one gear check the level and change the oil.<P><BR>Later||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||07-23-2000||09:57 PM||||Mine used to do that until I bled the crap out of the clutch hydraulics.  After a long Interstate drive (20-40 miles) it was almost impossible to get the clutch to disengage.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||07-23-2000||10:51 PM||||Sounds like a clutch dis-engagement thing.<BR>I recently switched to Redline,after draining the 90W that was in there originally,then to the GM syncromesh fluid,and like that the best.Since it cost the same as the Redline,I figured it was worth a try.<BR>Another good tip from a forum member prompted me to try it out.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||penetrator||07-24-2000||08:17 AM||||Strange?<BR>I was strictly told to not use anything else than GM manual gear fluid? And i got a problem when i have been driving a really long ride. When it gets hot it starts to sound really strange, like the gears are threading over(but the car still draging(accelerating)). <BR>So can i really change the oil to engine oil?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||2birds||07-24-2000||11:34 PM||||Muncie-Getrag 5-speed, OEM for all V-6, 5-speed Fieros, use 5W-30 motor oil, IAW the ownners manual and the plastic washer under the transaxle dipstick.  I just replaced mine with havoline full synthetic, and I don't think it's any better than the normal havoline I've run forever.  Might shift easier up North in the winter, but not my concern.||||reg||1
